fieldValues.summary:
Read by the diagonals (owner, vignette cad03157), each line of a domain holds the compass axes of one modality, since opposite cells share one. The diagonals are Cardinal {Versioning and Reference, Attribution and Repository}, Fixed {Identity and Assertion, Succession and Conformance} and Mutable {Description and Governance, Containment and Portability}. clerk domains (2026-10-28) shows Semantic records placing:
- Action: Attribution and Repository (Cardinal) and Description and Governance (Mutable, set aside);
- Change: Identity and Assertion and Succession and Conformance (both Fixed);
- Perspective: Containment and Portability (Mutable) and Versioning and Reference (Cardinal).
The domain's own three axes are one per modality (Attribution and Repository on Action, Identity and Assertion on Change, Containment and Portability on Perspective), which reads Action as Cardinal and Perspective as Mutable. By that reading, Versioning and Reference belongs on Action and Description and Governance on Perspective.
